    /* A previous attempt scaled the whole app up on wide viewports with CSS zoom. Reverted:
       zoom is a legacy, non-standard property with real Chromium compositing bugs for
       position:fixed content — every full-screen overlay in this app (title screen,
       LessonReader, StoryReader, TourOverlay, boss battle) uses position:fixed, and under
       zoom they paint as corrupted, tiled fragments even though getBoundingClientRect
       reports correct-looking layout geometry. Confirmed live: a "Full lesson" modal
       rendered as a duplicated, half-width mess with its close button unreachable. Bigger
       desktop sizing needs a different mechanism (e.g. portalling fixed overlays out of a
       scaled subtree) — not attempted here, since correctness matters more than a nice-to-have. */
